{
  "original_id": "win-00062-p02",
  "archive_id": "BW2-B62-P02",
  "title": "The Maximum Popular Dimension on Tied Unweighted K3,3 Is Two",
  "batch_label": "62",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every one of the 13^6 labelled weak-order preference profiles on the unweighted complete bipartite graph K_{3,3}, with every acceptable partner strictly preferred to being unmatched and with all 34 partial matchings admitted as alternatives, there is a popular-winning singleton or a popular-winning unordered pair of distinct matchings. Moreover, the profile ((0,0,0),(0,1,2),(0,2,1),(0,2,1),(1,2,0),(1,0,0)) has no popular-winning singleton. Therefore the maximum popular dimension over the frozen domain is exactly 2.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
